From 65fc70d5a128c1e68a4c9d5d668267cb846d5c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Troy Sargent <0xalpharush@protonmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:31:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(certify): scope cut-point stages to kept functions

certify.py turned cut-point (loop) proofs off whenever --exclude left
functions out, so a contract with loops could be scoped only by giving
up its loops. The cut-point simulation now takes the call predicate:
Runs/Scope.lean defines scope from the excluded selectors, the entry
relation of every stage carries scope call, the entry segment opens it
into the selector hypotheses that prune the excluded paths, and the
stage, composition and execution theorems are stated at scope.
---
 solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py | 38 ++++++++++++++++++---
 tools/certify/certify.py        | 58 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

